  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Troggu. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Troggu (Trogga) is a Swiss Tarot game from the German-speaking Valais. Uses a modified 62-card Tarot deck. 3-8 players. Features bidding (Normal/Solo), Tapp exchange, the unique Fool as highest trump, and Misere when all pass. The secret partner mechanic (calling a trump card) adds intrigue in 7-8 player games.',
    objective: 'Score 58+ of 114 card points (as declarer) or prevent it (as defenders).',
    gameplay: 'Bid: Pass/Normal/Solo. Tappist exchanges with Tapp (no 5-pt cards). Solo plays without exchange. Follow suit; must trump if void. Fool = highest trump (special last-card rule). 7-8 players: Tappist calls a trump for secret partner.',
